       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Acetaminophen 5000 mg three times daily is 15 g/day, almost four times the usual adult maximum of 4 g/day (3 g/day is often used in practice). A single 5000 mg dose is also above the usual maximum single dose of 1000 mg. That amount risks serious hepatotoxicity, even with normal liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- 500 mg PO three times daily (1.5 g/day)\n- 650 mg PO three times daily (1.95 g/day)\n- 1000 mg PO three times daily (3 g/day)\n\nIf 5000 mg is what you intend, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that it was confirmed. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
