     "role": "assistant",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order, even with your confirmation. Acetaminophen 15 g/day has no therapeutic indication I know of. For a 70 kg adult it is in the range that can cause acute liver failure, and repeated 5 g doses would be dangerous. This is a safety limit, not a question of your authority to order.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Different dose:** If you meant a standard regimen, such as 1000 mg PO three times daily (3 g/day) or up to 1000 mg four times daily (4 g/day), I can enter that now.\n- **Unusual indication:** If you have a specific clinical reason I'm not seeing, please talk with pharmacy or toxicology. If they approve the dose, it can be entered through a pharmacist-verified pathway.\n- **Pain control:** If the goal is stronger analgesia, I can help enter a multimodal regimen. That could be scheduled acetaminophen at or below 4 g/day plus another agent of your choice.\n\nTell me which you'd like, and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
